\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs24 Mayor Trantalis recognized Peter Partington, Infrastructure Task Force Advisory Committee (ITFAC) Chair, 1521 NE 53\super rd\nosupersub Street. Chair Partington discussed ITFAC's recommended Ordinance revisions. City Manager Williams said staff concurred with those revisions and read language clarifying that the Infrastructure Advisory Board (IAB) Ordinance applies to both existing and proposed City infrastructure and associated maintenance and improvement programs. The revisions also expand the IAB's scope to include bridges, stormwater systems, water and wastewater facilities, seawalls, roads, and sidewalks. City Manager Williams confirmed that the revisions could be incorporated into the Ordinance between the First and Second Readings.\cf1\f1\par
\par
Commissioner Beasley-Pittman inquired about the one (1) year terms of appointees. Mayor Trantalis questioned whether a short term would be effective and explained his reasoning. He suggested that longer terms would be more appropriate due to the complexity of infrastructure projects. City Clerk Soloman explained that board terms vary and are limited to six (6) consecutive years through reappointment. Further comment and discussion ensued. In response to Mayor Trantalis' request for a recommendation, Commissioner Beasley-Pittman suggested two (2) year appointments for IAB members, with the option for two (2) reappointments, totaling six (6) consecutive years.\par
\par
City Clerk Soloman clarified that the Ordinance amendments include two (2) year appointments for IAB members with the option for two (2) reappointments totaling six (6) consecutive years and ITFAC revision language read into the record by City Manager Williams that would be incorporated between the First and Second Readings. Mayor Trantalis confirmed.\par
\par
Commissioner Glassman introduced this Ordinance on First Reading which was read by title only.\par
}

