\viewkind4\uc1\pard\nowidctlpar\f0\fs24 In response to Commissioner Glassman\rquote s question, City Attorney McCartney confirmed that this Ordinance would do the opposite of what was just done by decertifying the district.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li2520\f1\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\f0 Commissioner Glassman made a motion to table, seconded by Vice Mayor Sorensen.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li2520\f1\par
\pard\f0 Mayor Trantalis recognized Sandy Fay, 1401 N 136th Avenue, representing Riverwalk Centre Ltd. Mr. Fay said a substitute avenue was promised to these establishments which would enable them to operate under the status quo and now it seems that avenue is being taken away. Mayor Trantalis explained that it is not being taken away; it is not being discussed at this time. In response to Mr. Fay\rquote s question regarding whether it will be discussed and implemented before the decertification goes into effect, Mayor Trantalis said he cannot answer because the Commission has not discussed and voted on it. After further discussion, Mr. Fay expressed his opposition to the motion to table.\cf1\f2\par
}

